{"ts":"2026-08-07T05:19:52.392Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"077176c9c9193448b4c63511","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.224","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-dqtzva"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The release gate classifies production errors by message prose and reads none of the 236 error codes the product declares, so every waiver is a latent re-block and a broad substring is a silent waiver"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The gate that decides whether production errors block a release partitions Sentry issues by lowercased message substring. It carries 34 hand-written patterns across four lists (8 console, 23 CLI, 1 validation, 2 environment) and references none of the 236 stable error codes the product declares, even though the handled-error channel already ships pm.error_code to Sentry as a tag and every refusal envelope carries a code and a urn:pm-cli:error type. Two failure modes follow and both are already realized in this repository. Latent re-block: message text is under no contract, so any wording change silently unmatches its pattern and re-blocks a cut; the file's own comments record that a per-count list re-blocked a release once a new count appeared, and the repair was to loosen the prose rather than to bind to a code. Silent over-waiver: broad substrings such as structural error(s) and item(s) failed to apply waive any future unrelated exception whose message happens to contain them, and no check asserts that a pattern still matches something or that it matches only what it intends. The asymmetry is inverted today: the release contract spec pins the allowlist pattern strings, so the waiver list is frozen while the messages it must match are free."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:ci","area:observability","gate","release"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-07T05:19:52.392Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-07T05:19:52.392Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The release error classifier decides from the declared error code and exit code, not from message text, for every family it waives; A check fails when a waiver entry matches nothing in the window, so a dead waiver cannot silently persist; A check fails when a waiver entry matches an error family it was not declared for, proving the waiver is not broader than its intent; Error messages become free to reword without touching the release gate, and a negative control proves a rewording no longer re-blocks a cut"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-c3uru0","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-07T05:19:52.392Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-ei6x66","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-07T05:19:52.392Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-x4nn3z","kind":"blocked_by","created_at":"2026-08-07T05:19:52.392Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-xp1xsw","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-07T0